WEBVTT

00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:15,630
I am a large filling that fell out of my wisdom tooth and it's been like that for over a year now.

00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:23,150
The back edge of the tooth is gone. I finally found a new dentist after insurance changed.

00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:29,870
Is it better to pull the tooth or get a crowd as far as health goes? I worry about

00:00:29,870 --> 00:00:38,990
cavitations with pulling the tooth and bacteria getting the tooth sealed in with a crowd.

00:00:39,630 --> 00:00:43,870
I know you're a dentist but I'm wondering if you have any insight. Well, it really depends on how

00:00:43,870 --> 00:00:54,590
much damage is to the tooth. It's salvageable. Yes, if you do get the tooth, if you just get it filled

00:00:54,750 --> 00:01:02,030
and they can build up the tooth with the filling, sometimes that's the best. Can you seal in bacteria

00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:12,830
by crowding it? It is possible. The worst is getting a root canal done because then the whole tooth

00:01:12,830 --> 00:01:21,550
is a hotel for bacteria. But usually if you have a crowd and it's a tight fitting crowd where there's

00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:31,070
no gap in the crowd, it's sealed with a sealant so there's no air in there. Then the chance of bacteria

00:01:31,070 --> 00:01:37,710
in there is much less. So again, I'd refer to your dentist in this. I don't have a dentist but

00:01:37,710 --> 00:01:43,870
is there a chance if you pull the tooth that you can end up with cavitations? Yes, if they do an x-ray,

00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:49,950
they're going to see how deep the roots are and that can be an issue. So yeah, just you're

00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:59,470
going to weigh all those things out. I think if the roots are strong enough and healthy enough

00:01:59,470 --> 00:02:05,710
and the tooth is still healthy other than that damaged part, get it filled and put a crown on so

00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:16,030
that you still have use of the tooth might be the best way to go.

